What are Atmospheric Gravity Waves?
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Atmospheric gravity waves (NOT gravitational waves from space!) are ripples
in the atmosphere caused by:
  • Mountains forcing air upward
  • Thunderstorm convection
  • Weather fronts
  • Jet stream instabilities

These waves create visible patterns like lenticular clouds and affect:
  ✓ Air pressure (oscillations)
  ✓ Temperature (periodic variations)
  ✓ Wind patterns (vertical motion)
  ✓ Precipitation (convective triggering)

How Do Gravity Waves Improve Rain Prediction?
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Research shows gravity waves are PRECURSORS to severe convective weather:

  1. Convection generates gravity waves
  2. Waves propagate outward from storm systems
  3. Wave signatures appear BEFORE heavy rainfall
  4. ML models can learn these patterns for early warning

11 New Features Extracted:
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
  📊 Brunt-Väisälä Frequency (atmospheric stability)
  🌡️  Temperature Perturbation Amplitude & Variance
  ⏱️  Dominant Wave Period (oscillation frequency)
  ⚡ Wave Energy Metric
  📉 Pressure Perturbation Amplitude
  📈 Pressure Tendency (rate of change)
  🌊 Pressure Oscillation Strength
  💨 Momentum Flux (wind-wave interaction)
  ☁️  Convective Source Term (CAPE, cloud tops)
  🎯 Wave Activity Flux (energy propagation)

Expected Benefits:
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
  ✓ Improved rainfall nowcasting (0-6 hour forecasts)
  ✓ Better detection of convective initiation
  ✓ Enhanced extreme rainfall prediction
  ✓ More accurate timing of precipitation events

